// 11 of 24, Finland loses about 5 of 10 ships a run, Sweden 4 of 11 (more than a Sverige's tonnage).
//   Sweden, the stronger ship: 283 mm guns, a 200 mm belt and 22.5 kn, and the transports to cover.
//   Finland, the numbers and the knife: big guns on small, slow, thin ships, and torpedo boats in the haze.
// The weather of the day: a thick midsummer haze on the Åland Sea (6 km), a light south-westerly.
